{
  "id": "santiago_herranza_mantaro",
  "name": "Santiago (Mantaro Valley cattle-marking songs)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "The Santiago, or herranza, is the cattle-marking fiesta of the Mantaro Valley in Junín, held around the feast of St James on 25 July, at which families mark and adorn their animals with ribbons to songs that call for the herd's increase. Women singers lead in a high, piercing voice while beating the tinya, a small hand drum, answered by the wakrapuku, a spiral trumpet built from joined cattle horns, and by violin. The membrane-drum card stands in for the tinya and the horns card for the wakrapuku.",
  "recipe": "classic modern santiago, ritual Devotional, indigenous branch. membrane drum pulse acoustic membrane drum, credited horns unspecified, fiddle. mountain valley. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
